  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Miserlou** (1 other source): Third song of Soulive's set: Marco Benevento joined on Rhodes and Kofi Burbridge played flute, after a trio start [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Miserlou**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Out On The Tiles**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **The Ocean**: back after 28 archived shows (805 days) [4]\n- **Elenor Rigby**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Get Back**: rare: 13 archived performances [4]\n- **Lucille**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Roll Out**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Butter Biscuit**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2010-03-12.flacf** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 154 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Saxophonist James Casey's band Six Figures opened; Nigel joined them for two songs, then technical problems caused a short pause [1]\n- Billed as day nine, with guests Derek Trucks, Susan Tedeschi, Oteil Burbridge, Marco Benevento, and The London Soul & the FELA Horns [1]\n- Oteil and Kofi Burbridge, Susan Tedeschi and Derek Trucks all joined the Soulive trio during the evening [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2010-03-12.flacf**: taped by BIGT AKA IAMHAMMERED; source: Onstage AT 833's -> Naint littlebox -> MicroTrack II 1/4\" line in Recorded at 24/48 [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by www.primevideo.com: [Prime Video: Bowlive: Live at the Brooklyn Bowl](https://www.primevideo.com/-/es/detail/0JRU3HG1LVE7ZHVZUBD69H63AS) [5]",
